# screen — postinst is root-only and unguarded (no `|| true`): it runs
# `install -g utmp -m 0775 -d /run/screen`, writes /etc/tmpfiles.d and a
# /lib/systemd/system symlink, and calls `update-rc.d`. None of that is
# reachable unprivileged, so `dpkg --configure` fails outright.
package  screen
install  unlikely
tier     never
note     root-only postinst (creates /run/screen, /lib/systemd/system, calls update-rc.d) — no unprivileged path; use the system's screen instead
